entry.summary:
If you've ever used MongoDB with n8n, you've probably hit this limitation. The MongoDB node in n8n doesn’t actually support real MongoDB update operations. Yeah… that surprised me too. The existing update functionality is extremely limited: Only allows updating a single field
Uses updateKey + value Internally tied to updateOne
That means no support for native MongoDB update operators like: $set (multiple fields) $pull $push $rename $inc Let’s say you want to remove a value from an array: { "$pull": { "tags": "deprecated" } }
👉 Not possible in the current node. Or update multiple fields: { "$set": { "status": "active", "updatedAt": "2026-01-01" } }
🧠 The Workarounds (that shouldn’t exist) Because of this, developers are forced to: Use aggregation pipelines 😬 Add…
